# Build-context hygiene for the backend image.
#
# The load-bearing rule is `app/*.json` below. Those files are the Instagram
# session (a live `sessionid` cookie — equivalent to being logged in as the
# official account) plus the link-code and seen-cursor state. They are
# gitignored, so a `git push` is safe, but `COPY app ./app` would still pull
# them into an image layer where `docker history` exposes them. Production state
# lives in Postgres, so the image never needs them.

# ── Secrets and account state ─────────────────────────────────────
.env
app/*.json
*.session.json

# ── Virtualenv ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~180 MB, and a different interpreter than the image's.
.venv/
venv/

# ── Bytecode and test artifacts ───────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
tests/

# ── Repo metadata ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml